# `mismatch`: an existential meeting a parameter that is not one is unpacked there into a
# fresh rigid type with its bounds as givens (Type System ch. 5, "Existentials are
# dictionaries"), so the two `any ^Eq` given to `Same`'s one `a` hide two types, and do
# not meet; `any ^Eq` has no `^Eq` of its own (Jimmy, 9 November 2026). `Same` of one
# hidden value with itself, through `Twice`, checks.
Same: fn a, a -> Bool where a: ^Eq
fn Same x, y = x == y

Twice: fn a -> Bool where a: ^Eq
fn Twice x = Same x, x

HideNat: fn Nat -> any ^Eq
fn HideNat n = any n

HideText: fn Text -> any ^Eq
fn HideText t = any t

Checks: fn Nat -> Bool
fn Checks n = (Twice (HideNat n)) and Same (HideNat n), (HideText "hi")
